-- title:
--   Finite part equals A-sections of the m-kernel scheme
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $p$ and $M$ with $p$ prime and $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a divisibility $p \mid M$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ lies in the non-units of $A$, and assume the residue field of $A$ has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed. Let $\Lambda$ be level data of type `JHNeronObjectAtP.LevelData p M H hpM A` — in particular it provides a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` compatible with the generic point, together with an auxiliary scheme over `base p` carrying a relative group law and dictionaries for its generic and special points — and let $O$ be a corresponding object of `JHNeronObjectAtP p M H hpM A hA Λ`, consisting of a scheme $G$ over `base p` with a commutative relative group law $O.L$, a bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ between $J_H(M)$ and the sections over the generic point, the smoothness, separatedness, finite type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity and connected-fibre properties of the structure morphism, Hecke correspondences, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by positive integers, and the remaining data of the structure. Let $m$ be a natural number. Then the cardinality of $O.\mathrm{finPts}\, m$ — the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by those $x$ which are killed by $m$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-curve `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and for which the generic section $O.\mathrm{pts}\, x$ satisfies the extension predicate `ExtendsToPlace A Λ.σA` — equals the cardinality of the set of morphisms $s \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to (O.L.\mathrm{baseChange}\, \Lambda.\sigma_A).\mathrm{schemeKer}\, m$ which are sections of the structure morphism $\mathrm{schemeKerStr}\, m$, the latter being the second projection of the pullback of multiplication by $m$ along the unit section, formed for the group law base-changed along $\sigma_A$.
--
--   This identifies the finite part of the $m$-torsion of $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$ with the group of $A$-valued points of the $m$-kernel scheme of the base-changed Néron object, the counting form of the description of the finite part of a Néron model over a henselian valuation base. It is used in the computation of the order of the finite part in terms of the relative sub-Picard data and in the comparison of toric points with the finite part.
